a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal; and
f. psychological services.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Regional Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.In the implementation of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with Government agencies, other Regional Governments and the community.
(3) Further provisions regarding procedures for services for handling the protection of women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 2

The implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence is carried out based on the principles of:

a. respect for human rights;
b. gender equality and justice;
c. non-discrimination;
d. the best interests of the victim; and
e. respect for the rights of women and children.

Article 16

Women and children victims of violence are entitled to the following rights:

a. right to be respected for their dignity and worth as human beings; b. right to physical and psychological recovery from the suffering experienced by victims;
c. right to make their own decisions;
d. right to receive information;
e. right to confidentiality;
f. right to social rehabilitation;
g. right to compensation;
h. right to complaint handling;
i. right of victims and their families to receive facilitation in the judicial process; and
j. right to assistance.

Article 17

Children who become victims of acts of violence, in addition to receiving the rights as referred to in Article 16, also receive special rights, as follows:

a. right to respect and full enjoyment for survival, growth and development;
b. right to basic services;
c. right to equal protection;
d. right to freedom from various stigmas; and
e. right to freedom.

Article 24

(1) Officials appointed to carry out integrated protection, services and recovery who fail to perform their obligations and responsibilities shall be subject to action and/or sanctions in accordance with the provisions of applicable Statutory Regulations;

(2) P2TP2A managers who, in carrying out the tasks of protection, services and recovery for victims of violence, violate the principles of implementing protection, services and 15 recovery may be subject to sanctions in accordance with P2TP2A internal mechanisms and sanctions in accordance with the provisions of applicable Statutory Regulations.

