e. fostering and supervising the implementation of protection for women and children victims of violence.
(2) In carrying out the obligations and responsibilities as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regent shall establish action programs and activities for the protection of women and children in one Regional Action Plan as the basis for SKPD in implementing the protection of women and children victims of violence.
(3) The Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), constitutes part of the Regional Medium-Term Development Plan.
(4) Further provisions regarding the Regional Action Plan as referred to in paragraph (2), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.

Article 9

(1) The Regional Government in an effort to prevent the occurrence of acts of violence against women and children shall carry out empowerment and awareness raising to families, parents and the community by providing information, guidance and/or counseling.

(2) In addition to empowerment and awareness raising as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government shall carry out efforts as follows:

a. improving the quantity and quality of education both formal and non-formal and informal;
b. opening accessibility to obtain education, training, funding, income improvement and social services;
c. creating job opportunities for women;
d. building community participation and awareness toward the prevention of protection for women and children from acts of violence;
e. building and providing a complete and easily accessible information system; and
f. building networks and cooperation with law enforcement apparatus, government apparatus, universities and various non-governmental organizations that work and/or care for women and children victims of violence.

Article 11

(1) Forms of services provided to women and children victims of violence, are as follows:

a. complaint services;
b. health services;
c. legal aid;
d. repatriation;
e. rehabilitation, social reintegration, and medicolegal; and
f. psychological services.
(2) Forms of services as referred to in paragraph (1), shall be implemented in accordance with minimum service standards established by the Regional Government and implemented by SKPD whose duties and functions are in the field of:
a. social affairs;
b. health;
c. women's empowerment and child protection; and
d. mental and spiritual.In the implementation of services as referred to in paragraph (1), the Regional Government may cooperate with Government agencies, other Regional Governments and the community.
(3) Further provisions regarding procedures for services for handling the protection of women and children victims of violence as referred to in paragraph (1), paragraph (2), and paragraph (3), shall be regulated by Regent Regulation.
